---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { operator, support, passes, passChoiceNote, passLengthNote, stackingNote, launchPricingNote, reminderNote, morTermsNote } from '../../data/payment';
---

<Base
  title="Terms"
  description="The terms for using the Rsquared Academy website, accounts and paid course tracks."
>
  <section class="sec" aria-labelledby="legal-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="legal">
        <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
        <h1 id="legal-h" class="t-h1">Terms</h1>
        <p class="t-small t-muted">Last updated: 13 November 2026</p>

        <h2 class="t-h3">About these terms</h2>
        <p>These terms are between you and {operator.legalName} ({operator.knownAs}), trading as Rsquared Academy, {operator.address.join(', ')}. By using www.rsquaredacademy.com or app.rsquaredacademy.com you agree to these terms.</p>

        <h2 class="t-h3">Using the site</h2>
        <p>Don't misuse the site: no attempts to break, overload or scrape it at scale, and no unlawful use.</p>

        <h2 class="t-h3">Accounts</h2>
        <p>Give accurate details when you create an account. One person per account, and don't share it. You are responsible for keeping your sign-in method secure and for activity on your account. You can ask us to delete your account at any time.</p>

        <h2 class="t-h3">Paid access</h2>
        <p>{passChoiceNote} All three cover all paid tracks. Each is a prepaid, one-time payment with no automatic renewal. The price and what is included are shown at checkout. See <a href="/pricing/">Pricing</a>.</p>
        <p>{passLengthNote} {stackingNote}</p>
        <p>{launchPricingNote}</p>
        <p>{reminderNote} Your progress is kept after your pass ends. Free courses stay free. Lessons 0–2 of every paid course are free to try before you buy. See <a href="/delivery/">Delivery and access</a>.</p>

        <h2 class="t-h3">Refunds</h2>
        <p>{passes.quarterly.exact} and {passes.annual.exact}: a full refund within 14 days of purchase if you have completed less than 20% of the lessons in every paid track (no single track at 20% or more). {passes.monthly.exact}: no refunds, except a duplicate charge or a technical problem we can't fix. The <a href="/refund/">Refund and cancellation policy</a> gives the full conditions and forms part of these terms. Nothing in these terms limits your legal rights.</p>

        <h2 class="t-h3">License and intellectual property</h2>
        <p>Site text, design, logo, course content, exercises, datasets and videos belong to Rsquared Academy. We grant you a personal, non-transferable, non-exclusive license to use the course content for your own learning during your access. You may not copy, resell, scrape or share credentials. Code you write yourself stays yours.</p>
        <p>Our eBooks, open course material and R packages are published under their own licenses, shown in each repository on GitHub; those licenses apply to them.</p>

        <h2 class="t-h3">Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>Don't abuse the code runner, submit answers automatically, or try to break the platform. Don't share accounts or course access with anyone else.</p>

        <h2 class="t-h3">Courses and changes to the service</h2>
        <p>The Foundations courses are free. Paid tracks open from 26 January 2027, with courses released in stages. We may update or retire content. If we withdraw a paid track during a {passes.quarterly.exact} or a {passes.annual.exact}, we refund the unused part of the period. Refunds for a {passes.monthly.exact} follow the refund policy above.</p>

        <h2 class="t-h3">Payments</h2>
        <p>Payments in India are processed by Razorpay. {morTermsNote} We never see or store full card numbers. See <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>.</p>

        <h2 class="t-h3">Links to other sites</h2>
        <p>We link to sites we don't control (for example GitHub, CRAN and YouTube). We're not responsible for their content or practices.</p>

        <h2 class="t-h3">No warranty</h2>
        <p>The site and its material are provided as is. We work to keep them accurate, but we don't guarantee they are complete, current or free of errors.</p>

        <h2 class="t-h3">Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>To the extent the law allows, Rsquared Academy is not liable for any indirect or consequential loss arising from use of the site.</p>

        <h2 class="t-h3">Suspension and termination</h2>
        <p>We may suspend or end accounts that break these terms. If we end your {passes.quarterly.exact} or {passes.annual.exact} for a reason other than a breach, we refund the unused part of the period. Refunds for a {passes.monthly.exact} follow the refund policy above.</p>

        <h2 class="t-h3">Governing law</h2>
        <p>These terms are governed by the laws of India. The courts at Bengaluru, Karnataka have exclusive jurisdiction.</p>

        <h2 class="t-h3">Changes and contact</h2>
        <p>We may update these terms and will change the date at the top. Questions: <a href={`mailto:${support.email}`}>{support.email}</a>, or see our <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> and <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> pages.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: var(--text-max);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .legal p,
  .legal li {
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
